# Clockie H2 + File Manager — External Web App Bridge Specification (v1.6)

Paste this prompt + specification into Google AI Studio (or any external web app) so it connects
cleanly via H2_CLOUD_BRIDGE v1.6 with prerender-safe activation, MV3 session persistence,
structured SESSION_EXPIRED recovery, real-time file/folder observation, optimistic concurrency
(revision / expectedRevision), lightweight stat, and binary Base64 transfer (e.g. SQLite databases).

================================================================================
Prompt for External Web App (Google AI Studio)
================================================================================
Implement support for the Clockie H2 Extension Bridge Protocol v1.6 (H2_CLOUD_BRIDGE):
- Zero-URL Session Binding (Critical):
  * Never read, write, or expect #h2Session or ?h2Session in window.location. The URL stays
    100% clean so SPA hash/path routing works untouched and URLs can be shared safely.
  * Store the active sessionId strictly in per-tab window.sessionStorage (for example key
    "h2_bridge_session_id"), never in localStorage.
- Strict v1.6 Startup, Prerendering & Page-Refresh Flow:
  * Always include protocolVersion: "1.6" on every request, and initiate connection with
    H2_CONNECT_REQ (protocolVersion: "1.6", supportedVersions: ["1.6"], clientName, and
    previousSessionId read from sessionStorage). All prior versions (v1.5 and earlier) and
    H2_HANDSHAKE_REQ are discontinued and rejected with reasonCode: "UNSUPPORTED_VERSION".
  * Content script injects at document_start and emits H2_BRIDGE_READY; H2_CONNECT_REQ also
    works immediately on page boot because listeners attach synchronously at document_start.
  * Chrome Omnibox / Speculation Rules Prerendering (New in v1.6): while document.prerendering === true,
    the content script defers H2_BRIDGE_READY and silently queues early H2_CONNECT_REQ calls until
    prerenderingchange fires on tab activation. The service worker also rejects any non-standard
    prerender connection with reasonCode: "PRERENDERING".
  * MV3 Persistence, Tab Replacement & Recovery (New in v1.6): active sessions persist in
    chrome.storage.session across MV3 service worker idle restarts, survive chrome.tabs.onReplaced
    tab swaps, and are protected against mid-load tabs.onUpdated races. If a session is ever
    invalidated (e.g. closed in Preferences or tab mismatch), Clockie H2 returns success: false with
    reasonCode: "SESSION_EXPIRED" across all request types so direct-mode clients can cleanly
    auto-reconnect once without string-matching error messages.
  * If the user opened this tab from the File Manager, the extension binds the launch to the
    browser tabId and returns H2_CONNECT_RES with sessionMode: "launched" and launchedScope
    (provider, rootName, launchedItemType, primaryRelativePath).
  * If the user opened the site directly — or refreshed the tab (F5) — the extension tears
    down the prior session, mints a brand-new sessionId (sessionMode: "direct", provider: "all"),
    and the app overwrites sessionStorage with the new sessionId for a clean fresh start.
- Real-Time File & Folder Observation:
  * Call H2_OBSERVE_FILE_REQ or H2_OBSERVE_FOLDER_REQ to subscribe to live change pushes
    (H2_FILE_CHANGED_EVENT / H2_FOLDER_CHANGED_EVENT). While >= 1 observation is active, the
    extension automatically holds a chrome.runtime.Port open with 20s heartbeats to keep the MV3
    service worker awake, and closes it once all observations stop or the tab closes/refreshes.
  * Watch quality by provider: Dropbox uses native longpoll ("cloud-push"), pCloud (/diff) and
    Google Drive (changes.list) poll at 4s ("cloud-poll"), Local Drive uses FileSystemObserver
    ("native") in the File Manager tab or 3s stat polling ("local-poll"). All mutations made
    through Clockie H2 bridge sessions or the File Manager UI are pushed immediately (0ms).
  * Echo suppression: every change event includes originSessionId (and originClientName).
    Compare event.originSessionId === client.sessionId to skip reloading your own saves.
  * Handle eventType === "resync_required" (emitted after SW restart/sleep-wake or cloud cursor
    reset) by re-statting or reloading the observed file/folder.
- Optimistic Concurrency & Clash-Free Writes:
  * H2_STAT_FILE_RES, H2_READ_FILE_RES, H2_SAVE_FILE_RES, H2_MOVE_FILE_RES, tree nodes, and
    change events return a normalized provider-agnostic revision string.
  * Pass expectedRevision on H2_SAVE_FILE_REQ (or expectedRevision: "NONE" for create-only).
    If another tab/device modified the file in the meantime, Clockie H2 rejects the write with
    success: false, reasonCode: "CONFLICT", currentRevision, exists, modifiedMs, sizeBytes.
- Binary Base64 Transfer & Size Guard:
  * For binary files (including .sqlite, .sqlite3, .db -> application/vnd.sqlite3), send and
    receive contentType: "binary" + encoding: "base64" (Uint8Array <-> Base64 string).
  * Single-message payload limit is 32 MB raw bytes (capabilities.maxPayloadBytes = 33554432);
    larger reads/saves fail cleanly with reasonCode: "PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE".
- Standardized Timestamps & Sizes:
  * All v1.6 responses and push events standardize on modifiedMs (epoch ms) and sizeBytes.
- Crypto Folder Protection (Always On):
  * Root-level folders containing "crypto" (case-insensitive) and encrypted pCloud items are hidden
    and permanently blocked across all read/write/create/delete/move/observe operations.
- Check accessMode ("readwrite" | "readonly") & capabilities before editing.

================================================================================
1. Unified Session Lifecycle (v1.6)
================================================================================
1. URL is always clean: https://your-app.example/#/any-spa-route
2. On boot: read prev = sessionStorage.getItem("h2_bridge_session_id"), clear it, and send H2_CONNECT_REQ
   with protocolVersion: "1.6", supportedVersions: ["1.6"], and previousSessionId: prev.
3. On H2_CONNECT_RES (success: true): save reply.sessionId into sessionStorage.setItem("h2_bridge_session_id", reply.sessionId).
   - If reply.sessionMode === "launched": open/focus reply.launchedScope (e.g. primaryRelativePath or folder tree).
   - If reply.sessionMode === "direct": show drive switcher for connected drives (reply.drives).
4. On page refresh (F5) or tab close: pagehide + tab listener tear down the old session & all active observations.

